# Android/F2FS hot data: small, frequently rewritten state.
# Shared 64-entry budget with f2fs-cold.list; extensions are 1-7 characters.
# Hot/cold are allocation hints, not guarantees about every app's workload.

# SQLite databases and their journal / write-ahead-log sidecars
# Explicit compound suffixes also work on kernels with exact matching.
db
sqlite
db-wal
db-shm
# Seven-byte limit prevents listing sqlite-wal and sqlite-journal.
# db-journal is also too long; db covers it only on prefix-matching kernels.

# Frequently rewritten caches, temporary files and diagnostic output
cache
tmp
temp
log
# Large streaming caches (e.g. exo) are intentionally not forced hot.
